WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:13.380
For a very short period of time, you were
the youngest person in the world.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:19.900
Until 1997, there were more pigs than people
in Denmark.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.740
Beetles often live within the fur of a sloth.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:29.490
A single sloth was discovered with over 980
beetles living in its fur.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:35.600
In 1993, San Francisco held a referendum over
whether a police officer called Bob Geary

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:41.420
was allowed to patrol while carrying a ventriloquist's
dummy called Brendan O'Smarty.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:42.440
He was.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:48.949
In 1923, jockey Frank Hayes won a race at
Belmont Park in New York despite being dead

00:00:48.949 --> 00:00:54.559
— he suffered a heart attack mid-race, but
his body stayed in the saddle until his horse

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:58.750
crossed the line for a 20–1 outsider victory.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:04.309
There is a village in Peru where people settle
the previous year's grudges by fist fighting.

00:01:04.309 --> 00:01:08.570
Then, they all start the new year off on a
clean slate.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:14.820
Kurt Cobain shot himself about one month after
Justin Bieber was born.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:21.260
In Washington DC, the Slovakian and Slovenian
embassies meet once a month to exchange wrongly

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.480
addressed mail.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:28.010
When the computer mouse was invented, it was
called the “X-Y Position Indicator for a

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.750
Display System.”

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:34.590
Until the 1800's, dentures were often made
from the teeth of dead soldiers.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:40.670
Tasmania, Australia has the cleanest air in
the inhabited world.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:47.250
When Coca-Cola announced the return of Coke's
original formula in 1985, ABC News interrupted

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.320
General Hospital to break the story.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:57.690
No one knows who invented the fire hydrant,
because its patent was destroyed in a fire.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:03.450
The northern leopard frog swallows its prey
using its eyes — it uses them to help push

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:07.950
food down its throat by retracting them into
its head.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:16.209
The first CD pressed in the US was Bruce Springsteen’s
“Born in the USA.”

